msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Max Auto-tune Example\n"
"\n"
"This example demonstrates how to use the `max_autotune` parameter in `torch.compile` to automatically search for the optimal configuration, thereby improving model performance.\n"
"\n"
"## Key Points\n"
"\n"
"- `max_autotune` will perform a more exhaustive search during compilation, which may increase compilation time, but can bring better runtime performance.\n"
"- You can use `torch.compile(model, mode=\"max-autotune\")` or `torch.compile(model, options={\"max-autotune\": True})` to enable this feature.\n"
"- For some models, `max_autotune` can significantly reduce inference latency, especially for those with many small matrix multiplications or convolution operations.\n"
"\n"
"## Code Example\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch.nn as nn\n"
"import time\n"
"\n"
"# Define a simple model\n"
"class SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__()\n"
"        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(784, 256)\n"
"        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(256, 128)\n"
"        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(128, 10)\n"
"        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n"
"\n"
"    def forward(self, x):\n"
"        x = self.relu(self.fc1(x))\n"
"        x = self.relu(self.fc2(x))\n"
"        x = self.fc3(x)\n"
"        return x\n"
"\n"
"# Create model and input\n"
"model = SimpleModel().cuda()\n"
"x = torch.randn(64, 784).cuda()\n"
"\n"
"# Compile using max_autotune\n"
"model_compiled = torch.compile(model, mode=\"max-autotune\")\n"
"\n"
"# Warm-up\n"
"for _ in range(10):\n"
"    y = model_compiled(x)\n"
"\n"
"# Benchmark\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"start = time.time()\n"
"for _ in range(100):\n"
"    y = model_compiled(x)\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"end = time.time()\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Average inference time with max_autotune: {(end - start) / 100 * 1000:.2f} ms\")\n"
"\n"
"# Compare with the uncompiled model\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"start = time.time()\n"
"for _ in range(100):\n"
"    y = model(x)\n"
"torch.cuda.synchronize()\n"
"end = time.time()\n"
"\n"
"print(f\"Average inference time without compilation: {(end - start) / 100 * 1000:.2f} ms\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Notes\n"
"\n"
"1. `max_autotune` may significantly increase compilation time, so it is recommended to use it in deployment scenarios where the model is compiled once and used repeatedly.\n"
"2. For some models, the performance improvement from `max_autotune` may not be obvious, or it may even lead to performance degradation. It is recommended to test it on your specific model.\n"
"3. In addition to `max_autotune`, PyTorch also provides other compilation modes such as `reduce-overhead` and `default`, which you can choose according to your needs.\n"

msgid "max_autotune 使用示例"
msgstr "max_autotune usage example"

msgid "`max_autotune` 是 Triton-Ascend 提供的增强自动调优装饰器，旨在简化多参数调优的代码编写。与社区版 `autotune` 要求用户手动枚举所有 `triton.Config` 不同，`max_autotune` 允许用户仅提供少量基础配置（如分块大小），并自动将相关的编译器选项（如 `num_stages`、`enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance` 等）纳入最优组合的搜索空间。用户也可以通过参数列表显式控制搜索范围。"
msgstr "`max_autotune` is an enhanced auto-tuning decorator provided by Triton-Ascend, designed to simplify the coding of multi-parameter tuning. Unlike the community version `autotune`, which requires users to manually enumerate all `triton.Config` entries, `max_autotune` allows users to provide only a few basic configurations (such as block sizes) and automatically includes related compiler options (e.g., `num_stages`, `enable_hivm_auto_cv_balance`, etc.) into the search space for optimal combinations. Users can also explicitly control the search scope through a parameter list."

msgid "**适用场景**：Ascend NPU 上的 `cube`、`mix`、`vector` 算子，尤其适合需要同时调整多个硬件相关参数的场景。"
msgstr "**Applicable Scenarios**: `cube`, `mix`, `vector` operators on Ascend NPU, especially suitable for scenarios where multiple hardware-related parameters need to be adjusted simultaneously."

msgid "基本使用示例"
msgstr "Basic Usage Example"

msgid "以下示例演示了使用 `max_autotune` 对一个简单的向量加法 kernel 进行自动调优。与社区版 `autotune` 相比，`max_autotune` 还会自动将不同的编译器选项纳入调优空间，无需用户手动指定。"
msgstr "The following example demonstrates the use of `max_autotune` for automatic tuning of a simple vector addition kernel. Compared to the community version of `autotune`, `max_autotune` also automatically incorporates different compiler options into the tuning space without requiring manual specification by the user."

msgid "import torch\\n"
msgstr "import torch"

msgid "进阶使用：精确控制调优参数"
msgstr "Advanced Usage: Precise Control of Tuning Parameters"

msgid "用户可以通过 **tuning_params 显式指定需要调优的编译器选项及其取值列表；未指定的参数会使用内置默认值。以下示例展示了如何对多个参数进行组合搜索。"
msgstr "Users can explicitly specify the compiler options to be tuned and their value lists via **tuning_params**; unspecified parameters will use built-in default values. The following example demonstrates how to perform a combined search for multiple parameters."

msgid "from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune\\n"
msgstr "from triton.backends.ascend.runtime import max_autotune"
